{"book":28,"chapter":1,"context":{"chapter":1,"title":"A Prophet's Marriage","summary":"God tells Hosea to marry Gomer, a woman who will be unfaithful, and to give their three children names that announce judgment on Israel, before promising that the judgment will be reversed.","background":"Whether Gomer was already promiscuous when Hosea married her or became unfaithful later is debated. Either way, the marriage mirrors God's covenant with Israel. Jezreel was where King Jehu had massacred Ahab's family; his dynasty, still ruling in Hosea's day, ended when Jeroboam II's son Zechariah was assassinated.","customs":[{"term":"Symbolic names","verses":"1:4-9","note":"Jezreel means 'God sows' and recalls bloodshed; Lo-ruhamah means 'not pitied' and Lo-ammi 'not my people.' Prophets' children sometimes carried messages in their names."}],"watchFor":["The sudden reversal: 'Ye are the sons of the living God' (v. 10).","Judah is spared for now (v. 7)."],"connections":["2 Kings 10:11","2 Kings 15:10-12","Romans 9:25-26","1 Peter 2:10"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["דְּבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] word of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["הוֹשֵׁעַ","hoshea'","H1954","HNpm","Hosea"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["בְּאֵרִי","be'eri","H882","HNpm","Beeri"],["בִּימֵי","bimei","H3117","HR/Ncmpc","in [the] days of"],["עֻזִּיָּה","'uziyah","H5818","HNpm","Uzziah"],["יוֹתָם","yotam","H3147","HNpm","Jotham"],["אָחָז","'achaz","H271","HNpm","Ahaz"],["יְחִזְקִיָּה","yechizkiyah","H3169","HNpm","Hezekiah"],["מַלְכֵי","malkhei","H4428","HNcmpc","[the] kings of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["וּבִימֵי","uvimei","H3117","HC/R/Ncmpc","and in [the] days of"],["יָרָבְעָם","yarave'am","H3379","HNpm","Jeroboam"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["יוֹאָשׁ","yo'ash","H3101","HNpm","Joash"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428